	(text "Observation input 23 into ${69119102-0ebd-473d-a7cb-d952bc88de42:REFERENCE} A1 (pin 2); leaves on contact 37." (at 670.76 334.01 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f107f5bf-4d4b-57db-b5ee-0ae5647a5b3a"))
	(text "Observation input 24 into ${f13cd1d5-28c7-4506-b50d-dbf0bfbd6248:REFERENCE} A8 (pin 9); leaves on contact 39." (at 670.76 346.71 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "bb04c44e-acef-5d03-a4b6-0bbcb2c3d802"))
	(text "Observation input 25 into ${f13cd1d5-28c7-4506-b50d-dbf0bfbd6248:REFERENCE} A7 (pin 8); leaves on contact 40." (at 670.76 359.41 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "2b65c3d4-7496-5927-9b40-b62252b4eed7"))
	(text "Observation input 26 into ${f13cd1d5-28c7-4506-b50d-dbf0bfbd6248:REFERENCE} A6 (pin 7); leaves on contact 42." (at 670.76 372.11 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "71e08faa-59d3-59f7-978b-0f5b62d54725"))
	(text "Observation input 27 into ${f13cd1d5-28c7-4506-b50d-dbf0bfbd6248:REFERENCE} A5 (pin 6); leaves on contact 43." (at 670.76 384.81 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f5f6e109-dec3-568a-968d-49e49c532852"))
	(text "Observation input 28 into ${f13cd1d5-28c7-4506-b50d-dbf0bfbd6248:REFERENCE} A4 (pin 5); leaves on contact 45." (at 670.76 397.51 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e05b69e2-4d8a-5557-958b-a2d016267045"))
	(text "Observation input 29 into ${f13cd1d5-28c7-4506-b50d-dbf0bfbd6248:REFERENCE} A3 (pin 4); leaves on contact 46." (at 670.76 410.21 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ac7ddaa5-8cc6-5841-a964-9c1195f44dfd"))
	(text "Observation input 30 into ${f13cd1d5-28c7-4506-b50d-dbf0bfbd6248:REFERENCE} A2 (pin 3); leaves on contact 48." (at 670.76 420.37 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6791d4e2-10f5-5da9-9bc3-f69cc1f998b7"))
	(text "Observation input 31 into ${f13cd1d5-28c7-4506-b50d-dbf0bfbd6248:REFERENCE} A1 (pin 2); leaves on contact 49." (at 670.76 433.07 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "0eb10906-d251-526e-8bf9-2693b8435233"))
	(polyline (pts (xy 15.24 398.78) (xy 226.126667 398.78)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "1705cd7d-b0ff-520f-af21-9ba1ca668ccd"))
	(text "OPERATION" (at 15.24 401.32 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "1763c7a1-c7e4-5a12-a03a-5a39cd0a3216"))
	(text "DUT side of the InstrumentPort-Digital-50 profile (board-interfaces docs/instrument-port-digital.md, draft v0.1). Direction is a hardware property, DUT to instrument only: DIGn enters ${7e0cdabf-d9e1-4b13-ab00-5a4417fdb564:REFERENCE} to ${f13cd1d5-28c7-4506-b50d-dbf0bfbd6248:REFERENCE}" (at 15.24 405.47 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "05cac517-bae0-5b14-8c10-e3083adcd50b"))
	(text "(DIG0 to 7, 8 to 15, 16 to 23, 24 to 31, each octet one package, A8 down to A1), leaves on Y8 to Y1 through 100 ohm damping (${fad54bc1-8b2f-4c3f-a18e-9b2430ab141a:REFERENCE} to ${b42723d6-d7f2-4621-8097-95df4034dcaa:REFERENCE}) onto ${27c0d602-bef6-4707-9c9a-9a3c429a569d:REFERENCE}. The cable carries no supply," (at 15.24 408.01 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b6288c90-1a35-5615-b387-b6925836b51d"))
	(text "reference, enable or stimulus." (at 15.24 410.55 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "cbed8060-51f9-5a20-b74a-58d845833e13"))
	(text "Pin mapping is the contract's DUT table and is not mirrored: channel n lands on contact 2 + n + floor(n/2) + floor(n/16), DIG0 on contact 2, DIG31 on contact 49, the 18 grounds on 1, 4, 7, ... 47, 50" (at 15.24 414.36 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "dfc38228-5f7e-5542-bc9d-962cccccead3"))
	(text "with the 25/26 double ground at the bank boundary. The mirror lives on instrument_port_digital_50_adapter_ffc_boundary_vertical; mirroring both ends cancels, and ERC and DRC cannot see it." (at 15.24 416.9 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "72393f30-8bcf-5e57-8db6-faf133e7adb7"))
	(text "Enabled by hardware default, no disable at all: both active-low enables of each package share one net held low by its 10 k pull-down (${84c143f8-b8f7-412f-b388-3f55d62abdd6:REFERENCE} to ${6c63e654-1b93-4601-99a7-45c9ca25760f:REFERENCE}; at most about 0.1 V from the two inputs'" (at 15.24 420.71 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "afc4cc2c-eb29-5441-8a46-7588ebca358e"))
	(text "leakage against the 0.99 V VIL), so observation works with the MCU in reset or unprogrammed. The contract permits this since 2026-09-15; do not re-add a control as a fix." (at 15.24 423.25 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6c6b756d-ef64-5887-9f0d-23bd25722aaf"))
	(text "Supply: the always-on 3.3 V rail on VCC (pins 20); SN74LV541A runs 2 to 5.5 V, drives +/-8 mA at 3.3 V, inputs tolerate 0 to 5.5 V with Ioff <= 5 uA unpowered, VIH 2.31 V, VIL 0.99 V, edges <= 100" (at 15.24 427.06 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c7ed3f21-f6e2-5402-8380-7236be4c97d5"))
	(text "ns/V, not a Schmitt input. ${32c854d3-e295-4ed0-ae67-c404202c33c2:REFERENCE} to ${97871112-ad18-45a1-a62c-deaacd916849:REFERENCE} (100 nF) bypass each pin 20; ${3b73245c-fad3-495c-87fd-b301079bbe35:REFERENCE} (4.7 uF, X5R 0402, well below nameplate at 3.3 V bias) is the one rail-entry bulk, not a fifth per-package bypass." (at 15.24 429.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c4df76a3-63ca-5331-8922-2a7c33628dda"))
	(text "The 100 ohm damping bounds a hard short of one output to GND at 33 mA, inside the +/-35 mA per-output absolute maximum, and damps edges into the cable; it is not short-circuit protection. Input" (at 15.24 433.41 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "639eee80-16ef-5406-b5f8-aa0b564786cd"))
	(text "bias is board-specific and not in this block: every unused DIGn must be tied at the board. Attach and remove the FFC with target power off; ${27c0d602-bef6-4707-9c9a-9a3c429a569d:REFERENCE} is rated 20 mating cycles, so break the link at the" (at 15.24 435.95 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e35765f1-0f41-5f44-90fe-857ca7a1a36c"))
	(text "instrument end." (at 15.24 438.49 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "754c402a-621c-5c38-98f5-7ba97f135bff"))
	(polyline (pts (xy 15.24 449.92) (xy 226.126667 449.92)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "8414fb8a-b7dc-5561-b8dd-1b1aae5ede27"))
	(text "DESIGN CONTRACT" (at 15.24 452.46 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "cd055f99-596a-597b-a5d5-08278438df93"))
	(text "DUT-side InstrumentPort-Digital-50 with integrated read-only buffering, on a VERTICAL, top-entry 50-contact ZIF connector: Hirose FH12-50S-0.5SVA(54), OW-CONN-FH12-50S-0-5SVA-54, LCSC" (at 15.24 456.61 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8e7bd436-8e63-5c20-aec0-86f48d7e17cb"))
	(text "C597991, 0.5mm pitch, symbol Conn_01x50, footprint orb_weaver_connectors:Hirose_FH12-50S-0.5SVA_1x50-4MP_P0.5mm_Vertical; the four mechanical lands are unnumbered pads and carry no net." (at 15.24 459.15 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "905dc3f7-6a0b-5db8-bf05-28bccdc0ea21"))
	(text "Thirty-two channels through four SN74LV541ARKSR octal buffers (OW-MISC-SN74LV541ARKSR, C7364695, symbol orb_weaver_misc:SN74LV541ARKSR, footprint" (at 15.24 461.69 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c3998de5-b8cd-5182-a064-27c60b43033f"))
	(text "orb_weaver_smd:Texas_RKS0020A_VQFN-20-1EP_2.5x4.5mm_P0.5mm_EP1x3mm, exposed pad 21 to GND), grouped DIG0-7 / DIG8-15 / DIG16-23 / DIG24-31 to match the 13-contact octet windows. The" (at 15.24 464.23 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c579fe9f-0b75-59a6-a380-75cf9224a566"))
	(text "541 is flow-through: input pin p pairs with output pin 20-p, A1(2) to Y1(18) through A8(9) to Y8(11). DIRECTION IS A HARDWARE PROPERTY: DUT to instrument only. The cable carries no supply, no voltage" (at 15.24 466.77 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c933799b-d077-5623-9682-168a38b488f6"))
	(text "reference, no enable and no stimulus, and nothing in this block may be driven by the instrument. PIN MAPPING IS THE CONTRACT'S DUT TABLE AND IS NOT MIRRORED: channel n lands on pin 2 + n +" (at 15.24 469.31 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "405058d5-6d31-51a4-b707-5806b38ac0e6"))
	(text "floor(n/2) + floor(n/16), so DIG0 is pin 2 and DIG31 is pin 49, with all 18 grounds on pins 1, 4, 7, 10, 13, 16, 19, 22, 25, 26, 29, 32, 35, 38, 41, 44, 47 and 50. THE MIRROR LIVES ON THE ADAPTER," (at 15.24 471.85 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a7c3d2e6-225b-5c6f-b2b9-a7b72a67ee2b"))
	(text "NOT HERE. instrument_port_digital_50_adapter_ffc_boundary_vertical is pre-mirrored to 51-n so that the expected reversing assembly - same-side Type A FFC with a vertical FH12 at both ends, connectors" (at 15.24 474.39 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b3ecee33-9b8e-5cc1-a7d1-cbe1b4f152ed"))
	(text "rotated 180 degrees - delivers DIGn to DIGn. Mirroring both ends cancels and channels arrive as DIG31-n. The ground pattern is palindromic under 51-n, so a mirrored map lands every ground identically" (at 15.24 476.93 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "84a9b19d-88d3-5295-b7bf-7bf2c4d247a8"))
	(text "and every net stays driven and terminated: ERC, DRC and design_block_tools.py check are ALL BLIND to this error, and only a pin-by-pin netlist comparison or continuity on the real cable catches it." (at 15.24 479.47 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d7b6fa6f-b024-5d8d-b020-fe3b206641ef"))
	(text "Per-output source damping is 100 ohms, OW-PASS-0402WGF1000TCE. That value is chosen as the smallest standard one that bounds a hard short to ground inside the LV541A's +/-35mA output absolute" (at 15.24 482.01 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3b213283-7b4e-5d99-9309-31ce1b751998"))
	(text "maximum even crediting the driver with zero impedance (3.3V/100R = 33mA); 68R gives 49mA, 47R gives 70mA, and the legacy 33R gives 100mA. It is NOT short-circuit protection and does not cover" (at 15.24 484.55 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5cf7630f-d0b9-5048-b2a7-6ebc44d52422"))
	(text "every fault. DEFAULT-ENABLED BY HARDWARE, AND THERE IS NO DISABLE AT ALL: both active-low OE inputs of each package share one net held low by a single 10k pull-down - ${84c143f8-b8f7-412f-b388-3f55d62abdd6:REFERENCE} through ${6c63e654-1b93-4601-99a7-45c9ca25760f:REFERENCE}," (at 15.24 487.09 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3aa34f56-f739-5ccf-98e8-02ef107f5c89"))
	(text "one per package - so observation works with the MCU held in reset, unprogrammed or unable to boot, and the port cannot be muted without desoldering. There is no manual jumper, no firmware link and" (at 15.24 489.63 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "40b14335-8ba5-507c-a50b-872bc895869d"))
	(text "no OE port. The owning contract was relaxed on 2026-09-15 from requiring manual disabling to permitting none, so this conforms; the reasoning and the retained future option are in" (at 15.24 492.17 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "48bb3c02-d431-53b4-a433-b901d4be255d"))
	(text "kicad-libs/docs/digital-instrument-port-design-blocks.md under 'No disable control, and why'. DO NOT re-add a control as an oversight fix. Shared 10k is verified against aggregate leakage: 2 x 5uA" (at 15.24 494.71 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9e1f6711-42d3-533f-8d88-cc1dbadf97bc"))
	(text "max gives 0.1V against a 0.99V VIL. If a noise investigation ever needs a mute, detaching the FFC bounds the cable's contribution but NOT the buffers', which keep switching into their board-side traces" (at 15.24 497.25 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "631907c0-b51e-5300-ac39-e722180733da"))
	(text "and damping resistors; lift the 100R resistors on the suspect channels instead. SUPPLY FROM THE BOARD'S ALWAYS-ON 3.3V RAIL, independent of firmware, HV_EN and every switched domain; a buffer on a" (at 15.24 499.79 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "02a7a249-423a-5217-94c7-4349b6e4db5b"))
	(text "switched rail cannot observe the domain it is powering down with. DECOUPLING is one 100nF per package, ${32c854d3-e295-4ed0-ae67-c404202c33c2:REFERENCE} through ${97871112-ad18-45a1-a62c-deaacd916849:REFERENCE}, hard against each pin 20 with a short return, plus one 4.7uF" (at 15.24 502.33 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "60a33792-331d-5e30-8871-48c50a096c77"))
	(text "rail-entry bulk, ${3b73245c-fad3-495c-87fd-b301079bbe35:REFERENCE} / OW-CAP-4U7-0402-X5R-16V, at the supply entry. ${3b73245c-fad3-495c-87fd-b301079bbe35:REFERENCE} is NOT a fifth per-IC bypass - do not 'fix' its distance to any package. Simultaneous-switching budget: 32 x 50pF" (at 15.24 504.87 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b05be102-e041-5aa2-81bc-7cee41de42af"))
	(text "x 3.3V = 5.3nC per all-channel edge, about 1mV of droop against the combined local reservoir. Expect meaningfully less than 4.7uF at 3.3V bias - a 4.7uF X5R in an 0402 derates hard - so treat the" (at 15.24 507.41 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "0ecd4d93-6037-51a1-b307-ea199b401fa1"))
	(text "nameplate value as nominal, not measured. INPUT BIAS IS BOARD-SPECIFIC AND IS NOT IN THIS BLOCK: there is no universal pull-down, because SPI selects, open-drain buses and switched-domain taps" (at 15.24 509.95 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "24a44ce8-2be4-5498-8917-71e932a50f44"))
	(text "each need different bias, and pulls that must read HIGH on a switched net reference the switched rail, never the always-on one. Every unused input must be explicitly tied at the board. LV541A at 3.3V" (at 15.24 512.49 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e0e00ba2-e10d-5faa-8333-e682f0f2930b"))
	(text "needs VIH >= 2.31V and VIL <= 0.99V with transitions <= 100 ns/V; it is 0-5.5V input tolerant with 2pF typical input capacitance and Ioff <= 5uA at VCC=0. It is NOT Schmitt-triggered and NOT a" (at 15.24 515.03 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "159a9aa7-650b-5841-b6ee-e9fdd58d738a"))
	(text "comparator: do not route a raw analog node through it for a timing witness, and do not treat a clean legacy LVC125A capture as LV541A qualification. OE would disable outputs only - it never removes" (at 15.24 517.57 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c0c27ad9-a9fc-5ea2-935f-b2b4dbe730bf"))
	(text "input loading or makes a floating input acceptable, which is part of why no mute was fitted. Requires straight-ended 0.30 +/-0.05mm FFC with gold contacts, at least 2mm exposed contact and 3mm" (at 15.24 520.11 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "095ed3b0-3751-5418-98db-62db8d6c51d7"))
	(text "reinforcement; retention-eared cable is NOT qualified for this connector. Rated 20 mating cycles, so prefer breaking the link at the instrument end, and attach or remove the cable with target power off" (at 15.24 522.65 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "655acec4-baa1-599e-8e38-eca1decbbf52"))
	(text "unless the actual assembly is hot-plug qualified. Profile is InstrumentPort-Digital-50 draft v0.1, UNQUALIFIED: no measured rate, delay, skew, loading or power-state limit has been established." (at 15.24 525.19 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "06e772ae-5352-55e3-85a6-7e65ac6896ce"))
	(text "Marker/beacon channel indices are NOT frozen, with DIG0/DIG1 the current recommendation over the earlier DIG14/DIG15. Pairs with instrument_port_digital_50_adapter_ffc_boundary_vertical; the" (at 15.24 527.73 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "2ee93b77-5108-5944-bb11-e02d0d029495"))
	(text "analyzer-specific channel map belongs to la5032_connector_boundary, not here. GROUNDED INPUTS ARE THE BOARD'S COPPER: the inputs are this block's ports, so a board that grounds unused DIGn" (at 15.24 530.27 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c80f0240-031f-578b-b211-f1a708a2ee11"))
	(text "channels draws one 0.20 mm track per grounded LV541A pad column straight into that package's thermal pad on F.Cu, before autorouting; Freerouting will not run a track along a row of same-net 0.5" (at 15.24 532.81 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ac2b1432-b0cf-5c9f-b97d-5a0e7855f065"))
	(text "mm-pitch pads and left those groups unrouted on every camera-board run (layout conventions 11a). Since 2026-09-29 every DIGn also ends at its own escape via above the pad row, so a board may" (at 15.24 535.35 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "0b0e2eff-1809-5e36-a6c0-ea912fa2377a"))
	(text "instead tie an unused channel to ground at that via; either way the grounding copper is the board's, never the block's. FLOOR COPPER IS DECLARED: the 0.10 mm gaps between the 32 damping resistors" (at 15.24 537.89 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d703ed57-e7d1-5d2f-850b-292999bfd109"))
	(text "and the LV541A pins (2026-09-26) and between each DIGn escape stub and the escape via beside it (2026-09-29) are wrapped in BLOCK_FLOOR rule areas, so a consuming board sees no clearance" (at 15.24 540.43 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "458aabfb-5d98-5438-a0ce-46878bea6b86"))
	(text "findings from this block under the shared rules; a board wanting 0.20 mm inside the block re-routes the block, not the rule (layout conventions 12)." (at 15.24 542.97 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "af9cdf4d-a119-5eb9-9ae7-f0e34542295e"))
	(group "Review page 01: 1. Octet DIG0 to DIG7: U39001" (uuid "0e4cbe78-b918-5775-be01-655291f456af") (members "32c854d3-e295-4ed0-ae67-c404202c33c2" "9ca2b7a3-7bc7-51c9-b422-38d45a9138a4" "58f855a1-30bd-5763-a948-dd5ceb193fd0" "e72a61c6-2bea-5488-86a6-bbac3f15e35d" "33fbc05b-88e0-5623-8751-3a467b0631c4" "84c143f8-b8f7-412f-b388-3f55d62abdd6" "05e0659b-aff3-55ca-b73d-b3938214fb9e" "58829689-6691-5b46-a8b3-da4b6d3368f8" "75baf473-23bc-573b-8e52-f5b397edfe97" "560b8515-7775-5174-b94d-cfd544eb40f7" "fad54bc1-8b2f-4c3f-a18e-9b2430ab141a" "349eda92-ae3e-5286-abc0-917969fd28c2" "01eba642-70cd-5615-94d6-0d43410edc1d" "65c3fcb5-ca38-5423-84f3-84d677c7825a" "7115e45d-fed6-5ee6-ac81-9ebc6ef6958d" "b1189718-aaad-4a24-9529-0c662c51e188" "d5125893-d912-5780-b908-b942fffac5d9" "4cce9995-3275-598f-9e17-be8a0994c2d2" "5996957c-6180-507f-98ed-b0d57a66a9fc" "caa6ba67-9e0b-5150-9eda-fad8ff1fd4a9" "48994ff4-4092-4dc3-ac54-ce78ec13af36" "ad8821a5-01f3-578f-9ac8-a57da8510a99" "94f79563-fca0-5cb0-b4ba-2166dd49d343" "c369eb00-2b75-5939-82f9-8a2d47784e0f" "cb3c99e2-2118-5adf-adf0-ac2b8165de04" "fa3ed363-fb6e-4364-82fc-d6772d24c155" "f9a5472f-d75a-5c99-ae22-5065d434d4c3" "04b47e30-d330-55aa-8730-43e1375c1637" "a7f522df-7244-56ef-8413-abda79a2a3f1" "2874aa91-cf77-5b06-84b4-ce173155e7d8" "29c319c0-b48a-4b60-b58d-3e37b97ee13c" "d8e968c0-0ba6-5221-8038-6c06594b7925" "300bab92-cb09-50d6-bc95-fc61eb36184b" "1ff27d5b-75d5-5c5d-8758-98d79a915f23" "a0f52a2e-ad71-50c2-b8d0-96585c93ed9e" "64747bab-e2a3-4789-89d9-f0b610efe164" "f1366fb5-a688-530b-8a99-f8278ebde57b" "307139d9-725f-53d3-9d30-df816dfcb392" "93d0df17-8e85-554e-90f8-f7422076a9fc" "4eea78c2-fd91-5126-838a-091c4ac1317f" "470b4aec-ef2a-4371-bf4f-14797c9bf765" "bee25923-02d8-55c4-be2e-b195f3dcc7d6" "c53c4033-cbc5-513f-aaca-376bad493b00" "0f03f862-96fc-5e7d-bc6e-c25d6704800a" "e95f4e81-a9f3-5b47-8510-9512c3cf30c9" "fcea49a0-ea4d-4aee-9697-0faa5db34934" "e76d4d36-5e76-5001-8d14-124c41a11c38" "247e5b5d-6fa9-5047-a468-9af56ad4e11a" "5a46da51-9186-52